# shadcn/ui usage

shadcn components are vendored into `components/ui/`. Treat them as **owned source code** — read and edit freely, but follow these conventions.

## Adding components

Use the CLI (config lives in `components.json`):

```bash
yarn dlx shadcn@latest add <component>
# e.g. yarn dlx shadcn@latest add card dialog input label form
```

Drops files into `components/ui/` using the `new-york` style and `zinc` palette.

## Using components

Always import via the `@/` alias:

```tsx
import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"
import { cn } from "@/lib/utils"
```

For polymorphic rendering (wrap a Button around a `Link` or `<a>`), use `asChild`:

```tsx
<Button asChild>
  <Link href="/foo">Go</Link>
</Button>
```

Merge classes with `cn()`, never raw template strings:

```tsx
<div className={cn("flex gap-2", isActive && "bg-primary")} />
```

## Theming

- Colors come from CSS variables in `app/globals.css` (`--primary`, `--background`, `--muted-foreground`, etc.).
- Use semantic Tailwind classes: `bg-primary`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`. Avoid raw color classes (`bg-blue-500`) unless intentionally going off-theme.
- Dark mode: add `class="dark"` to `<html>` (or use a theme provider). The `.dark { ... }` block in `globals.css` takes over.

## Variants

shadcn components use `class-variance-authority` (cva). To add a variant, edit the `cva` block in the component file — don't override at call sites with sprawling className strings.

## Don'ts

- Don't import Radix primitives directly from `node_modules` — go through `components/ui/` wrappers.
- Don't re-add a component from the CLI if you've customized it — it overwrites.
- Don't use Tailwind v3 syntax (`@layer` in `tailwind.config.js`). We're on v4 — config lives in `app/globals.css` via `@theme inline { ... }`.
